data.hmacresult#HmacResult:
type HmacResult = { hmac: Hmac | null; isSuccess: boolean; dateGenerated: Date; error?: unknown; }; error is present only on a failure and carries whatever was thrown — a missing scheme header, a private key that is not valid base64, crypto.subtle being unavailable outside a secure context.
It is typed unknown rather than Error because a catch binding is: anything can be thrown in JavaScript. Narrow it before using it.
if (!result.isSuccess) { const reason = result.error instanceof Error ? result.error.message : String(result.error); throw new Error(`could not sign the request: ${reason}`); }
